## Examples (MOST IMPORTANT)
- examples/toolkits/pptx_toolkit.py - Example usage of PPTXToolkit showing how to create PowerPoint presentations with an agent.
- examples/benchmarks/browsecomp_chat_agent.py - Example of creating a ChatAgent with a model, useful for agent setup reference.
- examples/workforce/multiple_single_agents.py - Example of setting up multiple single agents with different roles and tools, useful for agent orchestration patterns.
- examples/evaluation/single_agent.py - Example of a single agent usage script, useful for understanding single agent setup and usage.

## Implementation
- camel/toolkits/browser_toolkit.py - Implementation of BrowserToolkit and BaseBrowser for browser interaction and web agent simulation.
- camel/toolkits/pptx_toolkit.py - Implementation of PPTXToolkit for PowerPoint presentation generation.
- camel/agents/chat_agent.py - Base ChatAgent class (not read but implied from imports) for creating agents.
- camel/toolkits/__init__.py - Exports BrowserToolkit and PPTXToolkit among many other toolkits.

## Configuration/Types
- camel/types/enums.py - Contains ModelPlatformType and ModelType enums used for model configuration.

These files collectively provide the necessary components to create an agent with browser tools and PPT tools to search for information about CAMEL-AI and generate slides. The example in examples/toolkits/pptx_toolkit.py is especially relevant as it shows how to use PPTXToolkit with an agent, and camel/toolkits/browser_toolkit.py provides the browser interaction capabilities. The examples/workforce/multiple_single_agents.py shows how to combine multiple agents/tools which can be adapted for the task.
